/* Stroke-order data for the 216 characters Word Cards teaches — the 120 of
   the 第2级总字表 and the 96 NEW ones from the L1 认写字表 (新字): the outline
   of every stroke (s) and its centre-line (m), in the 1024-unit box the data
   is authored in, with y running UPWARD (the renderer flips it).

   PROVENANCE AND LICENCE. This is a 216-character subset of hanzi-writer-data
   (https://github.com/chanind/hanzi-writer-data), which derives it from the
   Make Me a Hanzi project (https://github.com/skishore/makemeahanzi), which in
   turn derives it from the Arphic fonts. It is used and redistributed here
   under the ARPHIC PUBLIC LICENSE, whose full text ships beside this file at
   the repo root as ARPHICPL.TXT. Modifications from upstream: only the
   characters Josh's deck teaches are included, and the per-character files are
   concatenated into this one so the page loads no extra request and works
   offline. Nothing about any glyph or stroke order has been changed.

   Hand-authoring this was never an option — 216 characters, up to 15 strokes
   each, and a wrong stroke order is a habit that has to be untaught. It is
   generated, so the one thing a future author must NOT do is edit a path by
   hand; re-derive it from upstream instead.

   Loaded with a <script src>, deliberately, rather than fetched: that is what
   puts it inside every derivation this repo already has — the service worker's
   precache scan, the offline boot test and the page-asset walk all read the
   page's own src attributes, and a fetch() is invisible to all three. */
